(167035, 9219, 2586, '<td valign="top">Just wanted to say that i like this image. The lighting isn''t so great (blown out on the ivy), shadow is nice but would have been more interesting at a deeper angle, and it would have been better if the red of the background would have been uniform in tone. But i do like the strong colors, the interesting, understated composition, and the props. You shot this as a portrait with the subject right smack in the middle. And that''s fine. If you had moved the subject over much more off-center and give a lot more negative space, the image would have become more intriguing and more zen-like (keep in mind this is coming from a zenner ;). Your score probably suffered somewhat from you picking a red background instead of going for more blue but i''m glad that you went for the red. Besides, the bottle is blue and the Ivy is indeed Blue Ivy :) so that should be enough but dpc voters love overkill. Congrats anyway on a very fine attempt. Journey</td>', 'Just wanted to say that i like this image. The lighting isn''t so great (blown out on the ivy), shadow is nice but would have been more interesting at a deeper angle, and it would have been better if the red of the background would have been uniform in tone. But i do like the strong colors, the interesting, understated composition, and the props. You shot this as a portrait with the subject right smack in the middle. And that''s fine. If you had moved the subject over much more off-center and give a lot more negative space, the image would have become more intriguing and more zen-like (keep in mind this is coming from a zenner ;). Your score probably suffered somewhat from you picking a red background instead of going for more blue but i''m glad that you went for the red. Besides, the bottle is blue and the Ivy is indeed Blue Ivy :) so that should be enough but dpc voters love overkill. Congrats anyway on a very fine attempt. Journey', '2002-12-09 01:07:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(167047, 9255, 472, '<td valign="top">alecia, this was one of my favorites.  great great job.  i had given this a 9! :)</td>', 'alecia, this was one of my favorites.  great great job.  i had given this a 9! :)', '2002-12-09 01:14:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(167055, 8994, 2923, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  The white stuff on top is both from JPEG noise and because the sun shines on it directly, reflecting the leaves.  This image can only be saved at 50% JPEG compression due to the 150kb limit and since it has a lot of details it can''t be saved within a reasonable quality.<br/> <br/>As far as what is a fractal -- a fractal is a simple mathematical formula that have a certain defined rules at a macro level, and the same rules applies at the micro level.  In this instance, the main trunk of the tree, spans into 2 branches, and each branches span into 2 more branches and so on and so on.  That''s a fractal-like pattern :)</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  The white stuff on top is both from JPEG noise and because the sun shines on it directly, reflecting the leaves.  This image can only be saved at 50% JPEG compression due to the 150kb limit and since it has a lot of details it can''t be saved within a reasonable quality. As far as what is a fractal -- a fractal is a simple mathematical formula that have a certain defined rules at a macro level, and the same rules applies at the micro level.  In this instance, the main trunk of the tree, spans into 2 branches, and each branches span into 2 more branches and so on and so on.  That''s a fractal-like pattern :)', '2002-12-09 01:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(167061, 9187, 1906, '<td valign="top">great. I dont know how anyone could complain....</td>', 'great. I dont know how anyone could complain....', '2002-12-09 01:24:08.000000', NULL, 0),
