(167079, 9150, 772, '<td valign="top">Phenomenal photo... i think it should have scored much higher... great work :)</td>', 'Phenomenal photo... i think it should have scored much higher... great work :)', '2002-12-09 01:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(167082, 9010, 1031, '<td valign="top">For the record, I have a common (in men) form of red-green color-blindness, which gives me difficulty in distinguishing between blues and purples, greens and browns, etc. I avoid making many judgements based on color -- I make my esthetic decisions primarily on tone, contrast, cropping, and sharpening, and the appropriate application of each considering the subject matter.<br/> <br/>When I checked some of the brightly-lit berries in Photoshop the densitometry indicated a pretty pure blue, although I''m sure there''s a lot of purple ones too.<br/> <br/>These were several feet up, and the wind was gusting that day 30-40mph and they were swaying pretty wildly, so I couldn''t really make it a much tighter shot. And, it <i>was</i> mostly back- and side-lit through the rest of the hedge.<br/> <br/>Privet berries are much esteemed by birds, but my gardening book makes no mention of their edibility by humans, so I''d suggest not eating any. It did mention that the fruit made a huge mess, so don''t plant over your patio or driveway. Privets are bushes or small trees used with great frequency for hedges.<br/> <br/>Thanks, everyone, for your comments. I think I actually scored a little better than I predicted!</td>', 'For the record, I have a common (in men) form of red-green color-blindness, which gives me difficulty in distinguishing between blues and purples, greens and browns, etc. I avoid making many judgements based on color -- I make my esthetic decisions primarily on tone, contrast, cropping, and sharpening, and the appropriate application of each considering the subject matter. When I checked some of the brightly-lit berries in Photoshop the densitometry indicated a pretty pure blue, although I''m sure there''s a lot of purple ones too. These were several feet up, and the wind was gusting that day 30-40mph and they were swaying pretty wildly, so I couldn''t really make it a much tighter shot. And, it was mostly back- and side-lit through the rest of the hedge. Privet berries are much esteemed by birds, but my gardening book makes no mention of their edibility by humans, so I''d suggest not eating any. It did mention that the fruit made a huge mess, so don''t plant over your patio or driveway. Privets are bushes or small trees used with great frequency for hedges. Thanks, everyone, for your comments. I think I actually scored a little better than I predicted!', '2002-12-09 01:35:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(167087, 8884, 4852, '<td valign="top">The title has little to do with the photo other that my 7th attempt at this setting, out of about 50 settings. <br/> It''s an antique medicine bottle filled with warm water. Set upon a crudely fashioned light box, over a blue filter. The laser was the tricky part at least the shape I came up with. I was trying to draw a circle around the BLUE bottle.</td>', 'The title has little to do with the photo other that my 7th attempt at this setting, out of about 50 settings.  It''s an antique medicine bottle filled with warm water. Set upon a crudely fashioned light box, over a blue filter. The laser was the tricky part at least the shape I came up with. I was trying to draw a circle around the BLUE bottle.', '2002-12-09 01:36:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(167107, 9029, 5212, '<td valign="top">A well-deserved first place.  Thanks for giving the shot info on your comment.  Did you have your camera set to Macro?  What focal length??</td>', 'A well-deserved first place.  Thanks for giving the shot info on your comment.  Did you have your camera set to Macro?  What focal length??', '2002-12-09 01:56:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(167110, 9214, 671, '<td valign="top">I had a number of people ask me WHAT IS THIS ANYWAY?  <br/>You know those electricity balls that you can put your hand on and lightning bolts come to your hand? This is one of those, only in the shape of the earth, complete with bumpy mountain ranges, etc.    I took it outside, draped it with black cloth, and took about 50 shots.  I did a little sharpening, but not much.  It looks fuzzy because it is a glowing ball, and it looks bumpy because it actually has bumps on it.  Sorry, no mystery!</td>', 'I had a number of people ask me WHAT IS THIS ANYWAY?  You know those electricity balls that you can put your hand on and lightning bolts come to your hand? This is one of those, only in the shape of the earth, complete with bumpy mountain ranges, etc.    I took it outside, draped it with black cloth, and took about 50 shots.  I did a little sharpening, but not much.  It looks fuzzy because it is a glowing ball, and it looks bumpy because it actually has bumps on it.  Sorry, no mystery!', '2002-12-09 02:02:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(167113, 9258, 811, '<td valign="top">I found your picture to be interesting.  I think the composition works well, and i suspected that the thing showing on the pillow was an album or something.  However, it was not identifiable, and I think that is what hurt your score.  After reading your description, the picture is obvious.  It was a great idea, and I look forward to seeing some of your other work.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'I found your picture to be interesting.  I think the composition works well, and i suspected that the thing showing on the pillow was an album or something.  However, it was not identifiable, and I think that is what hurt your score.  After reading your description, the picture is obvious.  It was a great idea, and I look forward to seeing some of your other work.   ', '2002-12-09 02:06:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(167115, 8994, 1031, '<td valign="top">Well I got your title, and think this is an excellent natural example. I like this even more now that I can read about how you did the color, as I''m a big fan of duotone mode, and look forward to trying this on one of my numerous shots of trees and sky.</td>', 'Well I got your title, and think this is an excellent natural example. I like this even more now that I can read about how you did the color, as I''m a big fan of duotone mode, and look forward to trying this on one of my numerous shots of trees and sky.', '2002-12-09 02:22:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(167134, 9181, 1019, '<td valign="top">Our family love your photo--definitely one of the best--well done and congrats on a great idea!!</td>', 'Our family love your photo--definitely one of the best--well done and congrats on a great idea!!', '2002-12-09 03:20:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(167148, 8984, 255, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b> <br/> <br/>this is really cool, what a great idea! it really does look like a crazily lit flower at first glance! the composition of this shot is almost perfect--i may have pulled out just a teeny bit more on the right. still, i love it. i love the contrasting blue and black colors. technically, very good considering the low light source. i wonder if opening the aperature would have helped any? dunno, but at any rate, the grain doesnt bother me at all, i think it works well here. all in all, this is a wonderful idea, very well executed! nice work! <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2002-12-09 04:06:29.</i></td>', 'CC  this is really cool, what a great idea! it really does look like a crazily lit flower at first glance! the composition of this shot is almost perfect--i may have pulled out just a teeny bit more on the right. still, i love it. i love the contrasting blue and black colors. technically, very good considering the low light source. i wonder if opening the aperature would have helped any? dunno, but at any rate, the grain doesnt bother me at all, i think it works well here. all in all, this is a wonderful idea, very well executed! nice work! ', '2002-12-09 03:53:06.000000', '2002-12-09 04:06:29.000000', 0),
(167150, 9218, 255, '<td valign="top">i just wanted to say how much i liked this! cant believe it didnt score better.</td>', 'i just wanted to say how much i liked this! cant believe it didnt score better.', '2002-12-09 03:54:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(167163, 8902, 255, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b> <br/> <br/>this is a really neat photo! i love the windmills and the background. they are sort of mystical, almost magical! compositionally, you did well. i really like how the still windmill is shoved to the right of the frame offset by the spinning one, very nice. the upward angle works really well here too--gives it a larger than life feel. technically, well done. the more i lokk at this photo, the more i am drawn in to the detail! very nice work!</td>', 'CC  this is a really neat photo! i love the windmills and the background. they are sort of mystical, almost magical! compositionally, you did well. i really like how the still windmill is shoved to the right of the frame offset by the spinning one, very nice. the upward angle works really well here too--gives it a larger than life feel. technically, well done. the more i lokk at this photo, the more i am drawn in to the detail! very nice work!', '2002-12-09 04:05:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(167176, 9014, 749, '<td valign="top">Well, I''m glad that <i>some</i> of you liked it... Yes, the sky was very grey, as it had been all week, and this was taken on the only day it wasn''t raining. The crop was primarily done like it is because there''s a streetlamp just below the bottom middle of this crop, and I wanted just the building, plus it put the upper two brickworks on the RoT points, so I was happy with that.<br/> <br/>I''m surprised that there weren''t any more blue-glass buildings in this challenge, but given my final score, I wonder if everyone else knew something I didn''t... ah well...</td>', 'Well, I''m glad that some of you liked it... Yes, the sky was very grey, as it had been all week, and this was taken on the only day it wasn''t raining. The crop was primarily done like it is because there''s a streetlamp just below the bottom middle of this crop, and I wanted just the building, plus it put the upper two brickworks on the RoT points, so I was happy with that. I''m surprised that there weren''t any more blue-glass buildings in this challenge, but given my final score, I wonder if everyone else knew something I didn''t... ah well...', '2002-12-09 04:19:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(167177, 9244, 255, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b> <br/> <br/>this has the makings of an awesome photo! the colors are fabulous and the composition great. i love the starkness of the branches against the sky, and then the contrast of the dark shadows against the white branches! i also really like how the trunks fan out in opposite directions and the smaller branches spread out to meet them---gives the whole picture sort of an "organized chaos" sort of feel! :)  i wonder if you had crouched down and shot more upwards if it would have looked even cooler? technically---this is where i am having a hard time. i feel like something is wrong but cant really place my finger on it? is it slightly out of focus? or is it oversharpened? i really cant tell because it just seems to make my eyes feel all jittery! other than that, however, it is a great photo! keep up the good work!</td>', 'CC  this has the makings of an awesome photo! the colors are fabulous and the composition great. i love the starkness of the branches against the sky, and then the contrast of the dark shadows against the white branches! i also really like how the trunks fan out in opposite directions and the smaller branches spread out to meet them---gives the whole picture sort of an "organized chaos" sort of feel! :)  i wonder if you had crouched down and shot more upwards if it would have looked even cooler? technically---this is where i am having a hard time. i feel like something is wrong but cant really place my finger on it? is it slightly out of focus? or is it oversharpened? i really cant tell because it just seems to make my eyes feel all jittery! other than that, however, it is a great photo! keep up the good work!', '2002-12-09 04:21:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(167182, 8995, 674, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>COMPOSITION  I liked the composition of this image but feel that the top could have had more cropped off it.<br/> BACKGROUND -  A little bit too grey on the left edge<br/> CAMERA WORK -TECHNICAL - Very good the shadow and impression of speed that the objects are giving has been very well handled, lighting is good<br/> DIGITAL PROCESSING - TECHNICAL -  The background blending is a bit uneven Top left corner darker grey than bottom and middle left.<br/>YOUR OPINION ON THE PHOTO - I thought this was a very good entry I gave it 8 overall <br/></td>', 'Critique ClubCOMPOSITION  I liked the composition of this image but feel that the top could have had more cropped off it. BACKGROUND -  A little bit too grey on the left edge CAMERA WORK -TECHNICAL - Very good the shadow and impression of speed that the objects are giving has been very well handled, lighting is good DIGITAL PROCESSING - TECHNICAL -  The background blending is a bit uneven Top left corner darker grey than bottom and middle left.YOUR OPINION ON THE PHOTO - I thought this was a very good entry I gave it 8 overall ', '2002-12-09 04:24:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(167190, 9207, 674, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>COMPOSITION - Composition was good CAMERA WORK -TECHNICAL - The glass and its contents were well lit and taken.<br/>YOUR OPINION ON THE PHOTO - this image was spoilt for me by the overpowering background which detracted from the main subject The blue fizz. I feel this shot would have placed higher with a more subtle background<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique ClubCOMPOSITION - Composition was good CAMERA WORK -TECHNICAL - The glass and its contents were well lit and taken.YOUR OPINION ON THE PHOTO - this image was spoilt for me by the overpowering background which detracted from the main subject The blue fizz. I feel this shot would have placed higher with a more subtle background ', '2002-12-09 04:33:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(167194, 9085, 4906, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I would have liked it a bit clearer too, was a tricky subject to focus on. I have a different version that I took a while ago that I feel is a better picture. See //www.pbase.com/image/6684988</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I would have liked it a bit clearer too, was a tricky subject to focus on. I have a different version that I took a while ago that I feel is a better picture. See //www.pbase.com/image/6684988', '2002-12-09 04:42:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(167195, 9227, 674, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/>COMPOSITION -CONTENT - I would have tried to have given more emphasis to the beautiful floor in this image and definitely not included that thing at the back that appears to have two headlights! I think a different angle might have helped to rid you of some of the distractions such as the blown out windows.<br/> CAMERA WORK -TECHNICAL - Exposure is not bad considering the difficult lighting<br/> DIGITAL PROCESSING - TECHNICAL -  Would have benefitted from some playing with the levels and usm as the image is a bit soft<br/>YOUR OPINION ON THE PHOTO - I wished that I could visit this beautiful place! <br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique ClubCOMPOSITION -CONTENT - I would have tried to have given more emphasis to the beautiful floor in this image and definitely not included that thing at the back that appears to have two headlights! I think a different angle might have helped to rid you of some of the distractions such as the blown out windows. CAMERA WORK -TECHNICAL - Exposure is not bad considering the difficult lighting DIGITAL PROCESSING - TECHNICAL -  Would have benefitted from some playing with the levels and usm as the image is a bit softYOUR OPINION ON THE PHOTO - I wished that I could visit this beautiful place!  ', '2002-12-09 04:49:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(167200, 9125, 255, '<td valign="top"><b>CC</b> <br/> <br/>i have gone out and taken shots like this myself! it is so hard to make our beautiful sky turn out like you see it! this really is a nice shot, the blue sky is a gorgeous periwinkle color, and the moon, small as it is, manages to make me feel very small! compositionally, it is nice. i like where you placed the moon and venus in the frame. technically, you did well, also. i guess the only thing that bothers me a little is the fact that it is almost "too" empty! i really dont mind the negative space feel at all, i jsut wish this one had a tad bit more in it to give it more impact. otherwise, very nice job!</td>', 'CC  i have gone out and taken shots like this myself! it is so hard to make our beautiful sky turn out like you see it! this really is a nice shot, the blue sky is a gorgeous periwinkle color, and the moon, small as it is, manages to make me feel very small! compositionally, it is nice. i like where you placed the moon and venus in the frame. technically, you did well, also. i guess the only thing that bothers me a little is the fact that it is almost "too" empty! i really dont mind the negative space feel at all, i jsut wish this one had a tad bit more in it to give it more impact. otherwise, very nice job!', '2002-12-09 05:13:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(167202, 9258, 4186, '<td valign="top">i didn''t vote on this image, but allow me to explain it to the people who didn''t exactly get it.<br/> <br/>the album is actually a 12 inch single, a song called "Lovesong" by The Cure (thus the title of the picture). it''s mine, btw. as is the bed.<br/> <br/>think about it for a second or two folks. lovesong. an empty, unmade, bed. i know it''s not blatantly obvious, not actually being the color blue, but that was NOT the challenge. just because you don''t get it, doesn''t mean it should get a low score. in fact, there should be points for subtlety, and making one think.<br/> <br/>brenna: i still woulda used this one: <a href="//www.pbase.com/image/8598410" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.pbase.com/image/8598410</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2002-12-09 05:38:49.</i></td>', 'i didn''t vote on this image, but allow me to explain it to the people who didn''t exactly get it. the album is actually a 12 inch single, a song called "Lovesong" by The Cure (thus the title of the picture). it''s mine, btw. as is the bed. think about it for a second or two folks. lovesong. an empty, unmade, bed. i know it''s not blatantly obvious, not actually being the color blue, but that was NOT the challenge. just because you don''t get it, doesn''t mean it should get a low score. in fact, there should be points for subtlety, and making one think. brenna: i still woulda used this one: //www.pbase.com/image/8598410', '2002-12-09 05:38:35.000000', '2002-12-09 05:38:49.000000', 0),
