(168446, 9094, 1280, '<td valign="top">I like this very much.  The crystal is interesting to begin with and the way you used light adds even more interest.  <br/>The background works perfectly.  Did you use fabric as a backdrop? What really adds intrigue is the various shapes, like the beams of varying blues radiating from near the upper left corner. My attention is drawn up to it, then it directs my eyes back to the subject.<br/>The circular curves also guide my eyes around the image. All the subtle shapes make up a great composition.<br/>The base of the crystal has a liquid appearance that is pleasing, and suggests motion, adding to the appeal.<br/>Technically everything seems to be in order...focus is good, exposure is very fine with good detail where needed. <br/>Overall you have combined good technique, interesting subject,  fascinating lighting, and wonderful diagonals and curves.  Ya did real good!  :-)<br/> <br/></td>', 'I like this very much.  The crystal is interesting to begin with and the way you used light adds even more interest.  The background works perfectly.  Did you use fabric as a backdrop? What really adds intrigue is the various shapes, like the beams of varying blues radiating from near the upper left corner. My attention is drawn up to it, then it directs my eyes back to the subject.The circular curves also guide my eyes around the image. All the subtle shapes make up a great composition.The base of the crystal has a liquid appearance that is pleasing, and suggests motion, adding to the appeal.Technically everything seems to be in order...focus is good, exposure is very fine with good detail where needed. Overall you have combined good technique, interesting subject,  fascinating lighting, and wonderful diagonals and curves.  Ya did real good!  :-) ', '2002-12-09 21:25:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(168460, 9019, 4162, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments everyone! Actually Fujisan is a few hundred kms away from where I took this, hence the haze, but on clear days you can see Fuji from all over the place.</td>', 'Thanks for all your comments everyone! Actually Fujisan is a few hundred kms away from where I took this, hence the haze, but on clear days you can see Fuji from all over the place.', '2002-12-09 21:29:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(168461, 8904, 554, '<td valign="top">should have been in top 10 at least</td>', 'should have been in top 10 at least', '2002-12-09 21:29:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(168512, 8885, 1280, '<td valign="top">The background works just fine in my opinion.  It supports the technical element introduced by the steel looking sharpener. I get the feeling that the pencil is being sharpened to perform and important function. No frills, just down to business.  <br/>The blue adds a touch of whimsie...a surprising bit of color. Of course the blue is essential to the challenge, but the way you incorporated it minimally works very well. <br/>The pencil shaving is perfectly shaped.  It lends a curve to the composition and is nicely placed well out of the center. The diagonal like leads right to that little bit of blue.<br/>Two things I''d like to point out that may be improved upon. First is that I''d like to see this a little lighter.  That could easily be improved in post-processing.  The other thing is the couple of flecks of debris from the pencil.  They are a minor distraction, but they do take away from the quality of the image.<br/>OVerall, this is a fine picture.  I love the simplicity of it and your execution is good.</td>', 'The background works just fine in my opinion.  It supports the technical element introduced by the steel looking sharpener. I get the feeling that the pencil is being sharpened to perform and important function. No frills, just down to business.  The blue adds a touch of whimsie...a surprising bit of color. Of course the blue is essential to the challenge, but the way you incorporated it minimally works very well. The pencil shaving is perfectly shaped.  It lends a curve to the composition and is nicely placed well out of the center. The diagonal like leads right to that little bit of blue.Two things I''d like to point out that may be improved upon. First is that I''d like to see this a little lighter.  That could easily be improved in post-processing.  The other thing is the couple of flecks of debris from the pencil.  They are a minor distraction, but they do take away from the quality of the image.OVerall, this is a fine picture.  I love the simplicity of it and your execution is good.', '2002-12-09 21:47:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(168550, 9065, 1280, '<td valign="top">Some of the detail seems to be lost.  Perhaps a different lighting might bring out some more of it. Lightening it in a photo editing program might work too.<br/>The composition is simple and straightforward and that is one of the fine qualities of this image.  The shape stands out nicely, though a little more contrast would make it really snappier.  I think the blue background is fine, but again with a little more contrast it would be sharper.<br/>OVerall this is nice, but needs a little snap to make it more appealing.</td>', 'Some of the detail seems to be lost.  Perhaps a different lighting might bring out some more of it. Lightening it in a photo editing program might work too.The composition is simple and straightforward and that is one of the fine qualities of this image.  The shape stands out nicely, though a little more contrast would make it really snappier.  I think the blue background is fine, but again with a little more contrast it would be sharper.OVerall this is nice, but needs a little snap to make it more appealing.', '2002-12-09 21:59:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(168556, 9143, 737, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique<br/>(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) - The subject is well chosen for the challenge. I like the simplicity and lines of the glass, as well as the few water drops. Well laid out, with off-center main subject.<br/>(2) BACKGROUND  I like the light colored background. It would be interesting to see a light blue sky as you said you were trying to get. It might have been too much. You might want to experiment with Photoshop and drop a blue sky in and see how it looks.<br/>(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Very good; focus is right on, good use of DOF in my opinion. Keeps eye focused on the glass, not reflection<br/>(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL -  excellent job. Good choice of white balance to bring out the blue.<br/>(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  well executed and good photo. I would guess that the score, while quite good, wasnt higher was because many people judged it as of medium interest.<br/> <br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Critique(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) - The subject is well chosen for the challenge. I like the simplicity and lines of the glass, as well as the few water drops. Well laid out, with off-center main subject.(2) BACKGROUND  I like the light colored background. It would be interesting to see a light blue sky as you said you were trying to get. It might have been too much. You might want to experiment with Photoshop and drop a blue sky in and see how it looks.(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Very good; focus is right on, good use of DOF in my opinion. Keeps eye focused on the glass, not reflection(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL -  excellent job. Good choice of white balance to bring out the blue.(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  well executed and good photo. I would guess that the score, while quite good, wasnt higher was because many people judged it as of medium interest. Jim msp', '2002-12-09 22:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(168592, 9158, 1280, '<td valign="top">Composition here is excellent, nice a simple.  Yes this is certainly art.  Art isn''t always understood.  It would be nice to see more detail about how you did this.  I think you used high contrast?  <br/>Anyway, I like it.  This should be framed and sold in a nautical shop.<br/>Tecnically I''d say this is very good work, however you processed it.  The color is good too.<br/>I like it!</td>', 'Composition here is excellent, nice a simple.  Yes this is certainly art.  Art isn''t always understood.  It would be nice to see more detail about how you did this.  I think you used high contrast?  Anyway, I like it.  This should be framed and sold in a nautical shop.Tecnically I''d say this is very good work, however you processed it.  The color is good too.I like it!', '2002-12-09 22:08:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(168599, 9040, 737, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique<br/>(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT)  Well constructed; fits challenge well. My only criticism would be on how busy it all looks. Id like to see some other variations, especially with shallow DOF to show only a couple of spools, with the rest in the background and slightly out of focus.<br/>(2) BACKGROUND  Though small, the black background sets off the subjects very well.<br/>(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Very good close up. Good DOF to bring everything into focus. Lighting looks good to me.<br/>(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  Well done. I see nothing to change.<br/>(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  Well executed, but very busy. Nothing here to wow the viewer, as others indicated.<br/> <br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Critique(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT)  Well constructed; fits challenge well. My only criticism would be on how busy it all looks. Id like to see some other variations, especially with shallow DOF to show only a couple of spools, with the rest in the background and slightly out of focus.(2) BACKGROUND  Though small, the black background sets off the subjects very well.(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Very good close up. Good DOF to bring everything into focus. Lighting looks good to me.(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  Well done. I see nothing to change.(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  Well executed, but very busy. Nothing here to wow the viewer, as others indicated. Jim msp', '2002-12-09 22:11:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(168617, 8904, 327, '<td valign="top">Thought this would score higher.<br/>?<br/>I like it.</td>', 'Thought this would score higher.?I like it.', '2002-12-09 22:16:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(168621, 9250, 1280, '<td valign="top">I love the subject.  The colors are vivid and perhaps too vivid.  The artsy look has an appeal but I''m not so sure it stands as straight photography.  I''m not saying you should do it any differently, but for this site it''s probably too artsy.  The processing left marks that look like they don''t belong, like on the stars.  <br/>The composition is neither divided into thirds or half.  It is somewher in between and could stand to be shifted into thirds.  The principle of thirds isn''t right for every picture and is sometimes relied upon too heavily, and adhered to too strictly.  But in my opinion, it would have worked well here. Show more of the stars on blue and a little less red and white stripes.<br/>Great subject!</td>', 'I love the subject.  The colors are vivid and perhaps too vivid.  The artsy look has an appeal but I''m not so sure it stands as straight photography.  I''m not saying you should do it any differently, but for this site it''s probably too artsy.  The processing left marks that look like they don''t belong, like on the stars.  The composition is neither divided into thirds or half.  It is somewher in between and could stand to be shifted into thirds.  The principle of thirds isn''t right for every picture and is sometimes relied upon too heavily, and adhered to too strictly.  But in my opinion, it would have worked well here. Show more of the stars on blue and a little less red and white stripes.Great subject!', '2002-12-09 22:17:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(168623, 8873, 714, '<td valign="top">I think this photo should have done alot better.  I like the framing and subject.  He could have lost his job or his wife left him.  He sure looks like he is feeling blue.  There is a tad bit of pink tint to the picture, but I kind of like it because of the effect it gives at the top of the photo.  It looks like the stress he is exserting.(sp)</td>', 'I think this photo should have done alot better.  I like the framing and subject.  He could have lost his job or his wife left him.  He sure looks like he is feeling blue.  There is a tad bit of pink tint to the picture, but I kind of like it because of the effect it gives at the top of the photo.  It looks like the stress he is exserting.(sp)', '2002-12-09 22:18:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(168624, 8924, 3280, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>Initially, I wasn''t sure what I was looking at. The texture of the snow seemed to throw me off a bit.  I like the feel of the shot and compositionally it is very good.  I have a problem with the black section at the top.  I think it sets the photo up well but the reflective "sparkles" in the  black seem out of place.  However, I think that overall the sparkles give this a magical feel.<br/> <br/>The other problem I have is with the twig/tree in the right foreground.  It seems to me that it could have been a bit more substantial to add to the photo. Color and lighting are very good. <br/> <br/>Overall, a very nice shot that certainly meets the challenge.  I don''t think it is quite a "wow" photo but ultimately belongs in the top 20% where it finished.  Nice Job!<br/> <br/>DougPaz</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! Initially, I wasn''t sure what I was looking at. The texture of the snow seemed to throw me off a bit.  I like the feel of the shot and compositionally it is very good.  I have a problem with the black section at the top.  I think it sets the photo up well but the reflective "sparkles" in the  black seem out of place.  However, I think that overall the sparkles give this a magical feel. The other problem I have is with the twig/tree in the right foreground.  It seems to me that it could have been a bit more substantial to add to the photo. Color and lighting are very good.  Overall, a very nice shot that certainly meets the challenge.  I don''t think it is quite a "wow" photo but ultimately belongs in the top 20% where it finished.  Nice Job! DougPaz', '2002-12-09 22:18:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(168628, 9129, 737, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique<br/>(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) - Almost excellent. You just needed to rotate a little to the left to include the whole man, not half. But you dont want to lose the door on the right. <br/>(2) BACKGROUND  Well done. I like the simple light colored wall, with the door on the right.<br/>(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL Very good focus &amp; DOF. Lighting gives a blue mood to the left side.<br/>(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  very good. No changes to recommend.<br/>(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  I like this better than most did. I like the simplicity, and the blue mood coupled with the blue clothes worn by the men. I think if you had captured the whole body on the left, you would have scored much better.<br/> <br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Critique(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) - Almost excellent. You just needed to rotate a little to the left to include the whole man, not half. But you dont want to lose the door on the right. (2) BACKGROUND  Well done. I like the simple light colored wall, with the door on the right.(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL Very good focus & DOF. Lighting gives a blue mood to the left side.(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  very good. No changes to recommend.(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  I like this better than most did. I like the simplicity, and the blue mood coupled with the blue clothes worn by the men. I think if you had captured the whole body on the left, you would have scored much better. Jim msp', '2002-12-09 22:20:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(168654, 9149, 3280, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>I liked this shot right from the first time I saw it.  IMO, this could have finished much higher than it did.  That is the risk you take when submitting an abstract shot.  The important thing is that you liked it.<br/> <br/>The composition is very good and I feel that your vibration certainly adds to the feel of the shot. The brightness of the lights to the left is a bit of a distraction.  I tried to look at a new crop but couldn''t really see one from what is here that would have worked within the rules. Perhaps you had more to work with in the original. <br/> <br/>Overall, I feel that this has an artistic feel that may not score well but more than meets the challenge. I actually scored it a 7 during the challenge.  Good job and keep it up!<br/> <br/>DougPaz</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! I liked this shot right from the first time I saw it.  IMO, this could have finished much higher than it did.  That is the risk you take when submitting an abstract shot.  The important thing is that you liked it. The composition is very good and I feel that your vibration certainly adds to the feel of the shot. The brightness of the lights to the left is a bit of a distraction.  I tried to look at a new crop but couldn''t really see one from what is here that would have worked within the rules. Perhaps you had more to work with in the original.  Overall, I feel that this has an artistic feel that may not score well but more than meets the challenge. I actually scored it a 7 during the challenge.  Good job and keep it up! DougPaz', '2002-12-09 22:35:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(168659, 9036, 737, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique<br/>(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) -  Good composition, straight on. I like the idea of using some unusual dress for the subjects. If they were working with you, I also would have taken a lot more shots in different positions, trying to get a composition that was a little more unusual  more fitting for the subjects. Perhaps off center some. I dont like the sign over his head. I like their coloring.<br/>(2) BACKGROUND  generally good. I like the blue tint. I dont like the sign over his head that is so bright, and possibly overexposed.<br/>(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Good. However, too many elements look over exposed, eg, her hat, his hands. Though f/4.4 should be ok. The focus around his face looks slightly off  perhaps he moved just a hair.<br/>(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  I assume the over exposure pieces are camera work, not post processing. If you use photoshop, adjusting levels &amp; curves might have helped.<br/>(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO A creative piece that could have done better, though I scored it above your average. I think the over bright areas could be toned down some, making this very good. In addition, moving them off center might help also.<br/> <br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Critique(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) -  Good composition, straight on. I like the idea of using some unusual dress for the subjects. If they were working with you, I also would have taken a lot more shots in different positions, trying to get a composition that was a little more unusual  more fitting for the subjects. Perhaps off center some. I dont like the sign over his head. I like their coloring.(2) BACKGROUND  generally good. I like the blue tint. I dont like the sign over his head that is so bright, and possibly overexposed.(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Good. However, too many elements look over exposed, eg, her hat, his hands. Though f/4.4 should be ok. The focus around his face looks slightly off  perhaps he moved just a hair.(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  I assume the over exposure pieces are camera work, not post processing. If you use photoshop, adjusting levels & curves might have helped.(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO A creative piece that could have done better, though I scored it above your average. I think the over bright areas could be toned down some, making this very good. In addition, moving them off center might help also. Jim msp', '2002-12-09 22:37:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(168674, 9046, 4162, '<td valign="top">I agree, I like it too! Thought it should have done better, but I suppose this kind of style doesn''t appeal to the masses.</td>', 'I agree, I like it too! Thought it should have done better, but I suppose this kind of style doesn''t appeal to the masses.', '2002-12-09 22:48:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(168682, 8903, 3280, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>You have the makings of a very nice shot.  The Fostoria glass is a beauty, especially the blue color which is made to order for this challenge.  <br/> <br/>Compositionally you have a few things you may want to look at.  First, the glass seems to be leaning a bit to the left. I find myself being led to the berries on the left of the photo and IMO they are a distraction.  The item on the right is not really identifiable and out of focus and also serves as more of a distraction than an addition to the shot.  Both of the items are casting unwanted shadows on your background.  There are also a number of light glares in your glass.  I count at least 12 which is also distracting.  You may want to try a shot where the shadow of the blue in the glass shows on the bottom of the shot.  It is a bit cluttered as is and takes away from your focal point.<br/> <br/>The blue glass certainly meets the challenge and I feel with a reshoot and a few new twists you have the makings of a really nice shot.<br/> <br/>DougPaz</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! You have the makings of a very nice shot.  The Fostoria glass is a beauty, especially the blue color which is made to order for this challenge.   Compositionally you have a few things you may want to look at.  First, the glass seems to be leaning a bit to the left. I find myself being led to the berries on the left of the photo and IMO they are a distraction.  The item on the right is not really identifiable and out of focus and also serves as more of a distraction than an addition to the shot.  Both of the items are casting unwanted shadows on your background.  There are also a number of light glares in your glass.  I count at least 12 which is also distracting.  You may want to try a shot where the shadow of the blue in the glass shows on the bottom of the shot.  It is a bit cluttered as is and takes away from your focal point. The blue glass certainly meets the challenge and I feel with a reshoot and a few new twists you have the makings of a really nice shot. DougPaz', '2002-12-09 22:52:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(168685, 9030, 737, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique<br/>(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) -  In my opinion, too dominated by the table, since I think you wanted the blue sky here. On the other hand, the wires, poles, and buildings on the far right detract. It would have been interesting if you had rotated to the right more, trying slightly different alignments. Having her off center slightly would probably help.<br/>(2) BACKGROUND  See above. The right hand area should be cropped out.<br/>(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Good focus &amp; DOF<br/>(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  I think a crop along the nearer tree on the right, and above the shadow on the table would make a great difference to this. Try a more portrait look.<br/>(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  I think I get the feeling you were after here  but a different cropping might have helped immensely, turning something above a snapshot into more of a photograph.<br/> <br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Critique Club Critique(1) COMPOSITION (CONTENT) -  In my opinion, too dominated by the table, since I think you wanted the blue sky here. On the other hand, the wires, poles, and buildings on the far right detract. It would have been interesting if you had rotated to the right more, trying slightly different alignments. Having her off center slightly would probably help.(2) BACKGROUND  See above. The right hand area should be cropped out.(3) CAMERA WORK ,TECHNICAL  Good focus & DOF(4) DIGITAL PROCESSING ,TECHNICAL  I think a crop along the nearer tree on the right, and above the shadow on the table would make a great difference to this. Try a more portrait look.(5) MY OPINION ON THE PHOTO  I think I get the feeling you were after here  but a different cropping might have helped immensely, turning something above a snapshot into more of a photograph. Jim msp', '2002-12-09 22:54:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(168710, 8871, 3280, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>My initial reaction to the shot was that it was a commercial Jet and I couldn''t understand the title.  Upon further review, I found the USAF on the wing and "got it".  I feel that this explains one of the problems with the shot.  It is hard to tell exactly what you are looking at.  I know how hard it is to get into position to take a shot of an airliner as I tried it last week for the Motion Challenge. However, a frontal or side view or even a landed military plane with the Wild Blue Yonder in the background may have told a better story.<br/> <br/>Your focus is excellent for a moving object (or I would have never been able to read the USAF!). IMO your negative space would have been much more effective if the cropping would have moved your subject out of the center of the frame.  Perhaps a little more contrast would have made the plane stand out against the sky too.<br/> <br/>Overall, the shot meets the challenge with the beautiful blue sky but needed a bit more oomph to do better in the challenge.<br/> <br/>DougPaz</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! My initial reaction to the shot was that it was a commercial Jet and I couldn''t understand the title.  Upon further review, I found the USAF on the wing and "got it".  I feel that this explains one of the problems with the shot.  It is hard to tell exactly what you are looking at.  I know how hard it is to get into position to take a shot of an airliner as I tried it last week for the Motion Challenge. However, a frontal or side view or even a landed military plane with the Wild Blue Yonder in the background may have told a better story. Your focus is excellent for a moving object (or I would have never been able to read the USAF!). IMO your negative space would have been much more effective if the cropping would have moved your subject out of the center of the frame.  Perhaps a little more contrast would have made the plane stand out against the sky too. Overall, the shot meets the challenge with the beautiful blue sky but needed a bit more oomph to do better in the challenge. DougPaz', '2002-12-09 23:05:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(168748, 9231, 3280, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!!<br/> <br/>I noticed that this is your first attempt at DP Challenge.  First and foremost, I hope that you will not be frustrated by your finish and not continue with the challenges. My first couple of shots didn''t do well either and I have learned so much in my time here.  <br/> <br/>A couple of fundamental problems with your shot.  The biggest seems to be your lighting.  It seems to be underexposed which in turn leads to graininess and lack of focus. The red glare on the right is also a big distraction. If I''m not mistaken, the Blue Cards are transparent so you might have shown a light through it to emphasize the blue color.  <br/> <br/>There is also a reflection of your camera on the card.  A definite no-no unless the photo calls for it. <br/> <br/>I like the angle that you used although you might want to crop out the number at the bottom.  All in all, the card certainly meets the challenge but you needed to bring out the blue color a little to confornm to the scoring.  Good luck in future challenges.  <br/> <br/>DougPaz</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!! I noticed that this is your first attempt at DP Challenge.  First and foremost, I hope that you will not be frustrated by your finish and not continue with the challenges. My first couple of shots didn''t do well either and I have learned so much in my time here.   A couple of fundamental problems with your shot.  The biggest seems to be your lighting.  It seems to be underexposed which in turn leads to graininess and lack of focus. The red glare on the right is also a big distraction. If I''m not mistaken, the Blue Cards are transparent so you might have shown a light through it to emphasize the blue color.   There is also a reflection of your camera on the card.  A definite no-no unless the photo calls for it.  I like the angle that you used although you might want to crop out the number at the bottom.  All in all, the card certainly meets the challenge but you needed to bring out the blue color a little to confornm to the scoring.  Good luck in future challenges.   DougPaz', '2002-12-09 23:21:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(168777, 9057, 4793, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all your kind and constructive comments, I was shooting under extreme conditions,windy and cold, and shooting in natural lighting,late afternon sun that was going away much to quick.</td>', 'Thank you for all your kind and constructive comments, I was shooting under extreme conditions,windy and cold, and shooting in natural lighting,late afternon sun that was going away much to quick.', '2002-12-09 23:30:57.000000', NULL, 0),
